4. Interview questions
Q1. Why must wait() be called inside synchronized code?

Because the calling thread must own the object's monitor; otherwise, Java throws IllegalMonitorStateException.

Q2. What is the difference between notify() and notifyAll()?

notify() एका waiting thread ला signal देतो, तर notifyAll() त्या monitor वर wait करणाऱ्या सर्व threads ना signal देतो.

Q3. Can wait() throw an exception?

Yes. It can throw InterruptedException, and it throws IllegalMonitorStateException if the thread does not own the monitor.

Q4. Does notify() release the lock immediately?

No. The notifying thread releases the monitor when it exits the synchronized section or method.